            pattern: ^https://.+
          autoStartMigration:
            title: Auto-start migration (M1 ANALYZE)
            type: boolean
            default: true
            description: 'When on (demo default), dest-init mints M1 ANALYZE, and M2 PLAN

              (child of M1) only when the scaffold''s .hermes/pins.json

              pins.planner.activation is "activated" (Operator GO after the

              planner activation gate). Never M3/M4 at dest-init.

              Turn off to inspect the workspace before agents touch it.

              '
          boardProtocol:
            title: Board protocol
            type: string
            default: outcome-board/v2
            enum:
            - serial-loop/v1
            - outcome-board/v2
            description: 'How the run''s work is organised after M2. outcome-board/v2

              (default) publishes every known outcome at M2 as a native Hermes

              Kanban task; Hermes owns the lifecycle (runs, dependencies,

              review and rework) under a cooperative local-worker model, and

              the migration''s domain checks guard each native action. It runs

              only when the platform has enabled it for this run (the

              migration-run provisioner records the selection and its execution

              state in the read-only run control), and a run that requested it

              never falls back to the serial loop: until the platform enables

              it, the launch refuses. serial-loop/v1 is the one-card-at-a-time

              loop, kept for explicit compatibility only. (outcome-board/v1,

              the protected-authority sidecar, is no longer offered to new runs.)

              Recorded once, in the destination''s initial commit; a run never

              changes protocol.

              '
